We are trying to create a Postscript preamble to allow Postscript
intended for the DEClaser 2150 and 2250 (the ln05R and ln06R) to run
on the HP LaserJet III and IIID with HP (true Adobe) PS cart.  We've 
had few problems so far, with the exception of not knowing what turns
the manual feed on for the DEClasers.

For the HP Adobe cartridge, the PS extensions section of the User's Guide
says manualfeed is a variable that should be set to true (for manualfeed on)
or false (for manualfeed off).  Simple enough. 

What is the extension that does the same for the DEClasers?  I've checked
the Adobe file server for PPDfiles for the DEClasers but they don't exist.

Can anyone quote me the paragraph or two in the DEClaser PS extensions 
chapter which describes manual feed?

Thanks,

--michael

P.S.    I would have thought that the extensions would have been the 
same for most of these printers using Adobe carts, but several seem to 
be different.  These mostly deal with what a paper tray is called.

